{"title":"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following fractions has the greatest value?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/5/fc5fdddb60d1e235da74d209231e086156cf182a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\frac{44444}{55555} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{5555}{6666} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac{666}{777} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{77}{88} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{8}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"499\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If a number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> repeated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> times divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> repeated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> times in terms of digits for some digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, then we realize that we can reduce the number to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. This is because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> repeated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> times for some digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> repeated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> times as a number multiplied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, which cancels out.\n</p><p>This means that answer choice A reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fd03d5b164ae8b40db27a6f8ddb20d9d43f95fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, answer choice B reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/5533bc48602603f16d18c04858cad119c04833c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, answer choice C reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84c09a22cab4593ee8a6a15fc2499a064c385559.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and answer choice D reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717366d5cd3f9573014d073ca33467c37c12a364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. Answer choice E is already in reduced form because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a>.\n</p><p>Of these answer choices, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/2/182b5f522183be1fa8b8db8fcda74a26386bb1d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } \\frac{8}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" /> is the largest. This can be verified with realizing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf16000eb8481c96669a9a67461472c5746acc92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{n + x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"49\" height=\"36\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/787bc36f403c92e2bb39954167099f1e7bda66ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n + 1}{n + x + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"81\" height=\"40\" /> for non-negative values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and positive values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), through converting the fractions into decimals, or by noting that each fraction is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minus some unit fraction, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594c8b267069448b58fe77ad60497eb30f763a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> is the smallest unit fraction for the answer choices.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley\">2017 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Cayley_P